From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haze <patches@haze.invalid>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:01:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Upgrade DNS to DNS over HTTPS automatically

Why: SPEC section 3 wants Secure DNS in automatic mode with Quad9, Mullvad and
Cloudflare to pick from. ungoogled turned the mode and the upgrade mapping off,
and domain substitution left the DoH probe asking for a name that never
resolves, so automatic mode could never upgrade. This restores the mode and the
mapping, probes example.com instead, adds Mullvad, turns Quad9's entry on and
shows only those three in the settings dropdown; the other providers keep
their upgrade mapping.
Security-relevant: yes
Security: Touches net/dns. Automatic mode falls back to plain DNS only where
it did before; the change makes lookups encrypted for users whose resolver
supports it. The probe sends one A query for example.com to the DoH server of
the provider the system already uses, and only for known providers; this is
listed in docs/PRIVACY.md and stops with Secure DNS off. Certificate checks
for DoH are unchanged.
Area: privacy
